==== hyperbricks yaml {!{page}} ====
# The YAML parser ignores this comment.
vars:
  route: pipeline

page:
  - type: <HYPERMEDIA>
  - route:
      var: route
  - title:
      config: site.title
  - guard:
      enabled: true
      auth:
        cookie: hb_session
      require:
        authenticated: true
  - hero:
      - type: <HTML>
      - value:
          format: |-
            # This comment stays because it is inside the block scalar.
            %s
          args:
            - file:
                base: resources
                path: hero.html
  - cta:
      - type: <TEXT>
      - value:
          env: CTA_TEXT
==== explainer ====
Pipeline fixture for the YAML source model. It shows preprocessing first, then materialization, then the runtime-facing Items pass.
==== expected preprocessed yaml ====
# The YAML parser ignores this comment.
vars:
  route: pipeline

page:
  - type: <HYPERMEDIA>
  - route:
      var: route
  - title:
      config: site.title
  - guard:
      enabled: true
      auth:
        cookie: hb_session
      require:
        authenticated: true
  - hero:
      - type: <HTML>
      - value:
          format: |-
            # This comment stays because it is inside the block scalar.
            %s
          args:
            - file:
                base: resources
                path: hero.html
  - cta:
      - type: <TEXT>
      - value:
          env: CTA_TEXT
==== expected materialized json ====
{
  "@type": "<HYPERMEDIA>",
  "@order": [
    "hero",
    "cta"
  ],
  "route": "pipeline",
  "title": "Pipeline Page",
  "guard": {
    "enabled": "true",
    "auth": {
      "cookie": "hb_session"
    },
    "require": {
      "authenticated": "true"
    }
  },
  "hero": {
    "@type": "<HTML>",
    "value": "# This comment stays because it is inside the block scalar.\n<section class=\"from-file\">\n  <p>File body</p>\n</section>\n"
  },
  "cta": {
    "@type": "<TEXT>",
    "value": "Start now"
  }
}
==== expected runtime json ====
{
  "ConfigType": "<HYPERMEDIA>",
  "Route": "pipeline",
  "Title": "Pipeline Page",
  "Items": {
    "@order": [
      "hero",
      "cta"
    ],
    "hero": {
      "@type": "<HTML>",
      "value": "# This comment stays because it is inside the block scalar.\n<section class=\"from-file\">\n  <p>File body</p>\n</section>\n"
    },
    "cta": {
      "@type": "<TEXT>",
      "value": "Start now"
    }
  }
}
==== expected output ====
<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta name="generator" content="hyperbricks runtime"><title>Pipeline Page</title>
</head><body># This comment stays because it is inside the block scalar.
<section class="from-file">
  <p>File body</p>
</section>
Start now</body></html>
